cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, and also cite TIGRE as listed in NOTICE."
title: "mlx-tomo: parallel-, fan- and cone-beam X-ray projection and backprojection on Apple GPUs via Metal/MLX"
abstract: >-
  Forward and backprojection operators for parallel-, fan- and cone-beam X-ray
  tomography on Apple silicon GPUs via Metal/MLX, with a TIGRE-compatible Python
  interface for supported operations. Provides Siddon and interpolated forward
  projectors, FDK-weighted and matched backprojectors, projection along
  arbitrary user-supplied rays for DRR generation, and FDK/FBP reconstruction.
  Host-side geometry is computed in float64 with a float32 GPU pipeline,
  validated against a float64 reference implementation and analytic phantoms.
  Volumes and projection stacks beyond 2^31-1 elements are handled
  transparently by slab and view splitting. Research software; not validated
  for clinical or diagnostic use.
type: software
authors:
